# Copy to .env (or export in your shell) and uncomment lines whose default
# ports conflict with locally running services. docker compose auto-loads .env.
#
# Naming follows each client's standard env var convention:
#   PostgreSQL  — libpq   (PGHOST, PGPORT, PGUSER, PGPASSWORD, PGDATABASE)
#   MySQL       — client  (MYSQL_HOST, MYSQL_TCP_PORT, MYSQL_USER, MYSQL_PWD)
#   MongoDB/ES/Redis — no standard port env; project-local names used
#
# Consumed by:
#   - docker-compose.yml         (dev DB services)
#   - src-tauri/tests/common/mod.rs
#   - e2e/fixtures/seed-smoke.ts (smoke seeding)
#
# E2E smoke has no entrypoint and nothing runs it in CI. Drive it by hand:
#   docker compose up -d postgres mongo
#   pnpm tauri build --debug --no-bundle --config src-tauri/tauri.e2e.conf.json
#   E2E_SPEC_KEY=postgres pnpm exec tsx e2e/fixtures/seed-smoke.ts
#   E2E_PG_PORT=15432 E2E_MONGO_PORT=37017 \
#     TABLE_VIEW_TEST_DATA_DIR=/tmp/table-view-smoke \
#     pnpm exec wdio run wdio.smoke.conf.ts --spec e2e/smoke/postgres.spec.ts
#
# The smoke run talks to DB services through host ports. The app under test
# stores its connections under TABLE_VIEW_TEST_DATA_DIR so the run does not use
# your normal desktop app data directory.

# ---- PostgreSQL (dev + smoke) ----
PGPORT=15432
# PGUSER=testuser
# PGPASSWORD=testpass
# PGDATABASE=table_view_test
# E2E_PG_HOST=localhost
# E2E_PG_PORT=15432

# ---- MongoDB (dev + smoke) ----
# MONGO_USER=testuser
# MONGO_PASSWORD=testpass
MONGO_PORT=37017
# E2E_MONGO_HOST=localhost
# E2E_MONGO_PORT=37017
# E2E_MONGO_DB=table_view_test
# E2E_MONGO_AUTH_DB=admin

# ---- E2E app data isolation ----
# TABLE_VIEW_TEST_DATA_DIR=/tmp/table-view-smoke

# ---- Host port overrides ----
# REDIS_PORT is live: docker-compose.yml publishes redis on it and
# e2e/fixtures/seed-smoke.ts seeds through it. Do NOT set it to 16379 — that is
# seed-smoke.ts's default Valkey port, and the two would collide.
# MYSQL_TCP_PORT / ES_PORT are read by nothing committed today.
# MYSQL_TCP_PORT=13306
# ES_PORT=19200
# REDIS_PORT=6379
